---
// import { published } from "@data/post"

import Wrapper from "@components/Wrapper";
const { frontmatter } = Astro.props;
---

<meta charset="utf-8">
<Wrapper title="Disjunctions" noindex={true}>	
	<div class="relative grid grid-cols-12 w-full md:px-[5%]">
		<div class="flex flex-col text-block max-w-[90ch] mx-auto font-serif col-span-full md:col-span-8 md:col-start-3">
			<h1>about us</h1>
			<p><i>Disjunctions</i> is a magazine run by critical researchers and practitioners of science and technology. We work to author, translate, and publish work that engages with today's digital realities and the ways society and technology reorganise one another. <i>Disjunctions</i> aims to create points of convergence for work seeking to critique capitalism's specificities in the digital age, across diverse geographies and polities. We aim to chart paths beyond technological determinism and the fetishisation of technical artefacts, towards a horizon where technology contributes to human dignity and freedom.</p>
			<p></p>
			<h1>editorial</h1>
			<p>We welcome contributions that span a wide range of themes, including: theoretical engagements with technology and labour; ethnographies of digital environments and their underlying material and infrastructural conditions; analyses of how contemporary technologies might reconfigure the structuring of knowledge and social order; investigations of technoscientific development in the global South(s); and practical resources — such as guides, manuals, or manifestos — that aim to oppose, subvert, or re-imagine configurations of technological hegemony.</p>
			<p>If you're interested in writing for us, please send your pitches or finished articles to <a href="mailto:editorial@disjunctionsmag.com">editorial@disjunctionsmag.com</a>. To pitch, send us two to three paragraphs about your prospective article, and a few sentences about yourself. Shorter contributions or reports tend to span 1,500–2,000 words; longer articles that engage with a topic in a more substantial fashion can take up to 5,000.</p>
			<p>We aim to respond to all inquiries within two working weeks, but since we often receive more pitches than we can handle, our ability to respond to everyone is at times limited.</p>
			<p>Submitted pieces should be written in an essayistic style rather than academic; please read through work we have published for an indication of what this should look like. We use British English, with a simplified version of Chicago-style citations. While we provide extensive editorial feedback, articles that require less editorial labour are likelier to be accepted and published on time.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Wrapper>
